IMPORT prelude

-- Duties Act 2001 (Qld) baseline -- the date arithmetic the other modules share, kept in one small module.
-- It uses only the prelude's DATE builtins (no daydate library).
--
-- READING (Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) s 38, not deposited): a period "within N days after" a day excludes that
-- day, so its last day is the day N days later; a period "within 1 year after" a day ends on the first anniversary of
-- that day. An anniversary of 29 February in a year that is not a leap year is taken as 28 February.

§ `Dates`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` `n` `days after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

-- Both days counted, as s 153(2) (OD) and TAA s 54(2) count them.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` `both inclusive` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the last day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day` PLUS 1

-- Called in prefix form: `is on or before` a b (the stable l4 rejects an infix call after AND or OR).
GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on or before` `a` `b` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is before` `a` `b` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `a` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier date of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS
    IF `is on or before` `a` `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `y` IF
        `y` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0
    AND (    (NOT (`y` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  `y` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` `n` `years after` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` (DATE_MONTH `the day`) `the year`
    WHERE
        `the year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS `n`
        `the day of the month` MEANS
            IF      DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 29
                AND DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 2
                AND (NOT (`is a leap year` `the year`))
            THEN 28
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the day`

-- Days from one day to a later one (0 if the second is not later), for regulative-rule clocks.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the end` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the start`
    THEN DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`
    ELSE 0
